*  RED (s106) -- PB-1s SNAPSHOT ALIASING, THE MINIMAL FORM: 9 lines, IN MAIN, no DEFINE, no
*  function call.  A pattern-valued statement RE-EXECUTED AT THE SAME SITE (goto loop) that
*  accumulates an ALT arm holding a snapshot-deferred plain ref.  PB-1s mints ONE hidden
*  PATV$k global PER SITE (static g_snapctr at LOWER time, lower_snobol4.c ~1998), so every
*  iteration re-assigns the SAME cell while the already-built pattern objects still DEFER-read
*  it.  Manual p.86: each construction freezes ITS OWN value -- one cell per site cannot do that.
*  ⛔ PRE-EXISTING: SIG11 under BOTH arms of SCRIP_PAT_EAGER_CALL (=1 and =0) -- NOT caused by
*  the s106 eager-call fix.  Oracle: /home/claude/x64/bin/sbl -b <file>
        s = 'ab'
        mk = LEN(0)
LP      IDENT(s)                        :S(DONE)
        s POS(0) LEN(1) . c =
        mk = mk ('X' | c)               :(LP)
DONE    'ab' mk                         :F(NO)
        OUTPUT = 'MATCHED r3'           :(FIN)
NO      OUTPUT = 'NOMATCH r3'
FIN
END
